<title>UK: Pearson loses ground after New Year gains.</title>
<headline>Pearson loses ground after New Year gains.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Pearson Plc fell 21-1/2p to 757-1/2 by 1110 GMT as investors pocketed their gains after a strong performance last week, dealers said.</p>
<p>Traders said the stock went up too quickly after many analysts recommended it a &quot;buy&quot; in the New Year.</p>
<p>&quot;They had a cracking week last week. This is just a correction,&quot; one trader at a major investment bank said.</p>
<p>Trading volume was a light 689,000 by mid-morning.</p>
<p>-- Paul Carrel, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
